Job summary &nbsp;

The Event Operations Specialist - Registration is our Cvent specialist for external events and campaigns. You own the Cvent registration experience from start to finish: building registration sites, managing invitations and attendee data, supporting check-in at live events when necessary, setting up registration for events run by other team members, and making sure every, campaign, registration, and attendance record flows cleanly (and accurately) into Salesforce. You also manage your own portfolio of virtual events, and you act as the department’s project manager, keeping work organized and helping streamline how the team operates. You work closely with the email marketing team, the content team (copywriters, designers, and others), local offices, and event specialists to make registering for a Mercer Advisors event convenient, polished, and on brand. &nbsp;

Essential job functions &nbsp;

Cvent registration site build and administration &nbsp;

• Build and launch Cvent registration websites, forms, and confirmation pages for in-person, virtual, and hybrid events, using reusable templates that reflect Mercer Advisors branding. &nbsp;

• Partner with the content team (copywriters, designers, and others) on registration site copy, imagery, branding, and request, review, and approve assets so every site is polished and on brand. &nbsp;

• Partner with the email marketing team to align registration sites with invitation, reminder, and follow-up emails, coordinating timing, messaging, links, and registration tracking before each send. &nbsp;

• Configure Cvent registration paths with conditional logic, multiple attendee types (such as clients, prospects, guests, and team members), capacity limits, waitlists, and approval workflows. &nbsp;

• Test every Cvent registration site end to end before launch, proofing content, logic, confirmation emails, and reporting for accuracy. &nbsp;

• Serve as the Cvent power user for local events, maintaining account standards, templates, user access, and data integrity, and documenting the build process so others can follow it. &nbsp;

• Confirm registration pages and communications meet accessibility, privacy, and compliance requirements. &nbsp;

Attendee management and communications &nbsp;

